A||||4||Michael||85 GT Fastback Conv.||||5||
Z||000000||Michael||09-04-2000||10:27 AM||||Has anyone converted a GT notchback to a Fastback?  If so how hard was it and what were all the parts needed? Any info would be great...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-04-2000||10:44 AM||||You basically need the fast back clip.  And if you are fortunate enough to find one the same color as the rest of your car, you won't even have to paint it.  Many have done the swap and from what I've read its fairly easy.  You need to access the bolts that hold on the notchback clip on the inside of the car, which means removing the plastic pillar panels and headliner on the inside of the car.  Remove the side moldings to remove those screws, plus any other screws that hold the clip on.  Remove the old clip, install the fastback clip and reverse the procedure for install.<P>Difficulty level depends on the skill of the doer.  After you've done a few its easy.  I haven't done a swap so it hard.||||reg||6
Z||000002||alpha||09-04-2000||02:54 PM||||I did a fastback swap this summer....actually I did a swap every body panel and the complete interior swap. It really was not very hard. The hardest parts were not related to the fastback swap itself, but rather the other parts of the car (door alignment, roof removal etc.)... Anyway there are a couple sites which detail the whole conversion. The only thing which was not exactally as these sites said was I had to modify the brake light wiring slightly. I did the conversion on an 85 SE.... I think the 85 and 84s are not wired to have seperate turn signals, where as the later cars are. I could be wrong on this tho.<P>The URL's for the conversion sites are: <A HREF="http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/converting2fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/converting2fastback.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.net/showroom/fastback.html</A> <P>If you have any problems or questions I would be happy to help in any way I can. You can email me at: douglas_knight@umit.maine.edu<P>HTH and Best of Luck,<P>--Douglas knight||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||09-04-2000||07:59 PM||||If you aren't affraid to tear your car apart to look like this...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/img015(1)_3.jpg"> <BR>...and not freak out. <P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe<BR><B>KEEP THE EXCITEMENT ALIVE!!</B>||||reg||1
